entry.summary:
In this paper, we examine Lin's "On NP versus coNP and Frege Systems" [Lin25]. Lin claims to prove that $	ext{NP} 
eq 	ext{coNP}$ by constructing a language $L_d$ such that $L_d \in 	ext{NP}$ but $L_d 
otin 	ext{coNP}$. We present a flaw in Lin's construction of $D$ (a nondeterministic Turing machine that supposedly recognizes $L_d$ in polynomial time). We also provide a proof that $L_d 
ot\in 	ext{NP}$. In doing so, we demonstrate that Lin's claim that $	ext{NP} 
eq 	ext{coNP}$ is not established by his paper. In addition, we note that a number of further results that Lin claims are not validly established by his paper.
